<title>ISRAEL: American Israeli Paper Q1 net down.</title>
<headline>American Israeli Paper Q1 net down.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Israeli Paper Mills Ltd reported the following results to the Tel Aviv Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>			   (in thousands of shekels)</p>
<p>			   Q1 97	Q1 96</p>
<p>Revenue		  295,176    302,336</p>
<p>Operating profit	19,420     17,353</p>
<p>Net Profit		12,553     13,823</p>
<p>Note: In June 1996 the company sold 49.9 percent of its Hogla unit to Kimberly-Clark Corp. American Israeli Paper's 1997 results reflect the contribution from only 50.1 percent of Hogla.</p>
<p>($1=3.40 shekels)</p>
<p>-Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
</text>
